    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on **Taylor Ward**, who stands as our clear top-tier play with a dominant 71.19 score. Facing a favorable matchup against a left-handed arm, **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage (+9%), making him the engine of our offensive projection for 2026-07-11. Joining him as high-priority starts are **Bryce Harper** (61.09) and **Gavin Sheets** (58.77). **Bryce Harper** remains an elite anchor in the 3-hole against Mize, bolstered by an excellent xwOBA profile, while **Gavin Sheets** draws a favorable matchup against Trey Yesavage, providing significant efficiency despite his current status as a lineup-pending gamble.\n\nThe bench decision process was tightened by the scarcity of our stolen base targets; **Jung Hoo Lee** was the most difficult exclusion, finishing just shy of the active roster at 45.39. While **Jung Hoo Lee** profiles well, he was ultimately pushed out by the superior platoon utility of **Daulton Varsho** (57.94), who earns a massive +10% boost against right-handed pitching today. We are also closely monitoring **JJ Bleday** (56.54), who presents a high-upside play against Assad but carries a 39% rain risk that could compromise his game cap efficiency. Conversely, **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Jonathan Aranda** face uphill battles against elite arms in Yoshinobu Yamamoto and Logan Gilbert, respectively, resulting in lower efficiency scores that leave them hovering near our marginal start threshold.\n\nOur remaining roster, including **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, and **Lawrence Butler**, will be deployed to balance our 5x5 categorical needs, prioritizing plate appearances in favorable hitting environments. We continue to navigate the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** on the IL, limiting our depth and placing extra pressure on **Masyn Winn** and **Lawrence Butler** to provide defensive efficiency while we wait for the return of bench assets like **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Zack Gelof**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Tyler Freeman**. Any late-breaking lineup changes for **Daulton Varsho** or **Gavin Sheets** will be monitored to ensure no bench-worthy assets are left on the table during this critical stretch.",
